COMMENT ON TABLE public.allergen_tag_crosswalk IS 'Bridges public.allergen_dictionary.k (what intake parsing writes into client_allergies.allergen_key) to public.meal_tags.key where kind=''allergen'' (what the meal library was reviewed against). A row means: this client-side allergen IS represented in the library vocabulary and can be filtered on. NO ROW MEANS THE LIBRARY CANNOT PROVE SAFETY for that allergen — assemble_client_meal_plan() must refuse, not filter. Adding a row is a safety claim: only add one when every published meal has actually been reviewed for that allergen.';

